{
  "name": "Gamalielite Dream-Twister",
  "type": "npc",
  "img": "icons/svg/mystery-man.svg",
  "system": {
    "role": "Qliphothic Parasite (Gamaliel — Lesser)",
    "tier": 3,
    "factionId": "",
    "notes": "<p>A predator of the subconscious: swirling oily black-and-purple smoke, featureless except that its silhouette keeps subtly shifting to mimic whoever is looking at it, two points of cold white light where eyes should be. It slips into sleeping minds and turns dreams into personalized hells, drinking terror and despair, leaving its victims exhausted, madness-touched — or not waking at all. It rarely manifests physically. In the dreamscape, it is the landlord.</p><p><strong>Qliphah:</strong> Gamaliel, the Obscenities — the Hull of Yesod. The Foundation's dream-layer, polluted at the source.</p><p><em>Mal's note: 'Post watches in pairs and wake each other on a timer. It cannot twist a dream you refuse to finish.'</em></p>",
